   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "From 70 to 100",
   "texto": [
    "In France's standard French, **70–79** is formed with **soixante + 10–19**. **71** is used for **et**: **soixante et onze**; **73**: **soixante-treize**.",
    "**80** is said to be **quatre-vingts** with a final **s** when it goes alone. Del **81** al **89** se usa **quatre-vingt + 1–9**, sin esa **s**: **quatre-vingt-un**.",
    "Del **90** al **99** se usa **quatre-vingt + 10–19**: **91**, **quatre-vingt-onze**; **99**, **quatre-vingt-dix-neuf**.",
    "**100** is **cent**."
   ]
